ration ensuring  that every secondary school pupil is  tested  as they return and regularly thereafter  i again want to thank teachers pupils  parents who've worked so hard to keep  schools safe  and keep them open  we're also asking universities to reduce  the number of students who return  to campus in january prioritizing  medical courses  and others requiring face-to-face  teaching  and in all cases students should be  offered  two rapid tests when they return  all of these measures are in the end  designed to save  lives and to protect the nhs  and for that very reason i must  ask you to follow the rules uh where you  live  tomorrow night and see in the new year  safely  at home that means not meeting up with  friends or family  indoors unless they're in the same  household or support bubble  and avoiding large gatherings of any  kind  we are still in the tunnel of this  pandemic  the light however is not merely visible  uh thanks to an extraordinary feat of  british engineering if you like the  the tunnel has been shortened or we're  moving  faster uh through it and  uh that gives uh me great confidence  about  the the future in the spring so for now  let's redouble our efforts let's follow  the rules  protect our nhs and together  make 2021 a year in which we leave this  tunnel  behind us
 

